craco is a tool specifically for Create React App (CRA). If you are trying to use vite build inside a project set up for craco, they are going to fight each other, and that’s exactly why your dist folder is never being created.

Since you're on your PC, let's fix that script block to be consistent. Change it to this:

JSON
"scripts": {
    "dev": "vite",
    "build": "vite build --outDir dist",
    "preview": "vite preview"
}
Why this is the "Real" Fix:
Remove Craco: Your project is clearly trying to use Vite (based on your earlier errors), so we need to get rid of the craco references in the scripts. They belong to a different "engine."

Add --outDir dist: This tells Vite exactly where to put the finished website.

The "Start" Script: In Vite, the command to run the app while you're working on it is vite (which we map to dev), not craco start.

One last thing to check on PC:
Since you saw craco in your scripts, check if you have a file named index.html.

For Vite: index.html should be in your frontend folder (next to package.json).

For Craco/CRA: index.html is usually hidden inside a public folder.

If your index.html is inside a public folder, Vite won't find it. Move index.html out of public and into the frontend folder.

Once you've updated the scripts and moved that file, push to GitHub and Vercel should finally see that "dist" folder!

